        "original_id": "891a2c5e-ba00-5c8d-a59a-762d765db046",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: Operation Grenade, Lorraine Campaign\n- Organizations: U.S. Ninth Army, U.S. Third Army, U.S. Army historians\n- People: Lieutenant General William Hood Simpson\n- Places: Roer (Rur) river, Roermond, Düren, Lorraine\n- Topics: World War II\n\nFacts:\n- The Lorraine Campaign is the term used by U.S. Army historians for operations of the U.S. Third Army in Lorraine during World War II from September 1, 1944, through December 18, 1944.\n- In February 1945 during World War II, Operation Grenade was the crossing of the Roer (Rur) river between Roermond and Düren by the U.S. Ninth Army.\n- Lieutenant General William Hood Simpson commanded the U.S. Ninth Army during Operation Grenade.",
